  "explanation": {
    "en": "Each level had a northern name and a southern name. A province was a bhukti or a manḍala. A division was a viṣhaya or bhoga, or a koṭṭam or valanāḍu. A district was an adhiṣhṭhāna or paṭṭana, or a nāḍu. A group of villages, like a modern tahsīl, was a vithi, or a paṭṭalā or kūṛram."
  },
